  message: "Cross-item review 2026-05-17: investigation confirmed features[] is spec-documented as a stable public contract at docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:798-802 (named slices with id, query, stable-ID-from-query, entry_nodes, edge_ids), with consumer compatibility commitments at lines 1701 and 1717 ('Consumers MUST ignore unknown fields in features[]'). docs/schema.json:99 carries the JSON-Schema entry. The 100% empty state means implementation diverged from spec (hypergumbo slice writes separate slice.<entry>.json files instead of populating behavior_map.features), NOT that the field is dead. Description rewritten to reframe the choice as a design call: either implementation catches up to spec (slice machinery wired into the behavior-map builder, default feature-set per entrypoint) OR spec catches up to implementation (retire features[] from spec, schema, and producer; canonicalise separate slice files). The original 'kill the field' framing conflated 'producer empty' with 'design intent absent' — they're different concerns."  # 01d5
